  {
   "id": "_ov_wUcNBgAJ",
   "from": "Claudio Quezada R.",
   "author": "5b52119333a64131",
   "date": "2018-05-07T18:54:53Z",
   "subject": "Re: Mensaje privado sobre: [tRophicPosition-support] Posterior alpha",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Dear Martha<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">In the plot attached you have 2 consumers: SEI and SMI (or the same consumer in different locations, the interpretation is the same). Each consumer has different stable isotope Nitrogen values (first panel), but the mean trophic position is similar (around 3.5, second panel), although the 95% credibility interval is quite different for them. Also, the contribution of benthic and pelagic baselines are different <u>for each consumer</u> (third panel, bottom). In the consumer SEI the contribution of the first baseline is rather low, so the other baseline should be high. Please do not confound both consumers, this is an analysis <u>for each consumer</u>. In this plot, only the first baseline is shown.<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">In case of the consumer or location SMI, the first baseline contributes much more, but the 95% credibility interval goes from 0.25 to 1.00, suggesting there are not many samples (baselines and/or consumer stable isotope values) or they are highly variable.<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">If you have any questions, please let me know.<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Cheers<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Claudio<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><br>--<br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Dr. Claudio Quezada-Romegialli</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Profesor Asociado</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Departamento de Biología<br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Facultad de Ciencias Naturales y Exactas</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Universidad de Playa Ancha<br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Móvil: <a href=\"tel:+56%209%209038%200148\" value=\"+56990380148\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+56 9 9038 0148</a></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Teléfono: <a href=\"tel:+56%2032%20250%200519\" value=\"+56322500519\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+56 32 250 0519</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2018-05-04 12:56 GMT-03:00 Martha Rosas <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">m.patric...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span>:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Claudio<div><br></div><div>Thanks for your reply ... Please, let me understand. In my study, I want to determine the trophic position of a seal in two locations and for each location, I have two baselines (benthic and pelagic), so the &quot;posterior alpha&quot; shown in the plot (attached) reflects the contribution of the two sources in the consumer (if this is the case, why do I have a value close to zero in a locality?, that is, do not have any contribution of baseline on this locality?) or is it a reflection of the contribution of the pelagic baseline on the benthic baseline?.</div><div><br></div><div>Forgive me so many questions, but I want to understand the metrics of your model.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Best regards</div><div><br></div><div>Martha</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-Y_9L1uiHlzw/Wux-8urOgZI/AAAAAAAAPaA/UYkJieIey4gRopqpbOYK7lOJG8vNogfYgCLcBGAs/s1600/Figure%2B1.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-Y_9L1uiHlzw/Wux-8urOgZI/AAAAAAAAPaA/UYkJieIey4gRopqpbOYK7lOJG8vNogfYgCLcBGAs/s1600/Figure%252B1.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497508365000&amp;usg=AOvVaw24cxoVwhy5a8Fq-c2bzvXO\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-Y_9L1uiHlzw/Wux-8urOgZI/AAAAAAAAPaA/UYkJieIey4gRopqpbOYK7lOJG8vNogfYgCLcBGAs/s320/Figure%2B1.png\" width=\"320\" height=\"181\" border=\"0\"></a></p><div><br></div><div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
